github-keys prints the SSH public keys a user publishes on GitHub, for
sshd_config's AuthorizedKeysCommand, so that a machine can accept the keys
people already keep on their GitHub account without copying them anywhere.

It can also be chained after another key source: with chain_ssh_wrapper in
stns.conf it adds GitHub's keys to the ones an STNS server serves.

Only public keys are visible, because no credentials are sent, and one HTTPS
request is made per authentication attempt.
